# DTF tier manifest: ops-log-noise  (artifact-keeper#4552 / #4794, #4526 / #4798, 1.11.3)
# Profile-set: filesystem + upstreams.mock-ops (a slow file upstream and a
# refusing OCI registry on a per-slot 172.16.<slot>.0/24 subnet) +
# topology.two-replica (a second backend on the same Postgres and /data
# volume, both with PROXY_SINGLEFLIGHT_ADVISORY_LOCKS_ENABLED=true).
# Both fixes are log-level fixes, so the oracle asserts on `docker logs` of
# the backend containers (json-file driver, pinned by the mock profile and
# the topology profile).
#
# THE BUG (#4552, fixed by #4794)
# With cross-replica proxy single-flight on, the replica that loses the cold
# fill blocks on `SELECT pg_advisory_lock($1, $2)` until the leader publishes
# (designed behaviour: one upstream fetch cluster-wide). The wait ran on a
# pooled-then-detached connection with sqlx's default 1 s slow-statement
# threshold, so every waiting replica logged
#   WARN sqlx::query: slow statement ... SELECT pg_advisory_lock($1, $2) elapsed=...
# per cold object. The fix opens the wait session from the pool's connect
# options with slow-statement logging off and logs the outcome once at DEBUG.
# The oracle: replica A (host port) starts a Maven Remote GET of a 2 MiB file
# the mock streams over 4 s; 0.7 s later replica B (docker exec ... curl
# 127.0.0.1:8081) GETs the same path and waits on A's advisory lock.
#
# THE BUG (#4526, fixed by #4798)
# An OCI Remote without upstream credentials whose upstream refuses a manifest
# (401 / 403) answers the client 404 MANIFEST_UNKNOWN and logs the refusal
# once at INFO, but the catch-all of map_proxy_error also logged an unsampled
#   WARN Proxy fetch failed: Bad gateway: Upstream returned error status 401 ...
# on every pull. The fix logs that line at DEBUG for a refusal of a request
# that carried no credentials; credentialed refusals, upstream 5xx and other
# refusals (400) still WARN.
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1):
#   (FIX #4552)  no "slow statement" line naming pg_advisory_lock in either
#                replica's log for the contended fill. RED on 1.11.2.
#   (FIX #4526)  three pulls each of a 401 and a 403 manifest through the
#                anonymous OCI Remote log no "Proxy fetch failed" WARN. RED on
#                1.11.2 (one WARN per pull).
#   (CONTROL)    both replicas serve the file byte-identical to the upstream,
#                the upstream saw exactly ONE fetch (the lock-protected fill
#                ran once cluster-wide) and B waited for it (>= 2 s); every
#                refused pull still reaches the upstream and gets 404
#                MANIFEST_UNKNOWN; the INFO refusal line is in the log (the
#                log is read from the right container); a 400 refusal still
#                logs one "Proxy fetch failed" WARN per pull; a working image
#                still proxies its manifest byte-identical.
#
# Teardown after --keep: backend-b lives in backend's network namespace, so
# a bare `run.sh down --slot N` (base file only) cannot remove the stack. Use
#   harness/run.sh down --slot N --upstreams mock-ops --topology two-replica
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false so a 429 can never masquerade as either verdict.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock upstream is on a private subnet.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-ops topology.two-replica"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
